{"agent":"Monster3-DX-grok-hook-descriptor-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The `_meta.source` string states “the prompt field name is a guess,” but this fixture’s `stdin` contains no `prompt` field at all (only `hookEventName`, `sessionId`, `cwd`, `workspaceRoot`, `toolName`, and `toolInput`). The same false provenance note is repeated in `pre_tool.json:5` and `pre_compact.json:5`. This makes the fixture metadata incorrect: a maintainer or test that trusts the source note to locate or replace the guessed `prompt` field will be misled, and the fixture claims a guessed field that it does not exercise.","digest":"61822b8d853d3fda","location":"tests/fixtures/harness/grok/post_tool.json:5","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/fixtures/harness/grok/post_tool.json:5"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The fixture asserts a normalized `prompt` value even though its own metadata says the raw prompt field name is only a guess and is not part of the documented field list (`prompt.json:5`). This makes the test suite encode an unverified third-party fact as an expected normalization result. For example, if the real Grok `UserPromptSubmit` payload uses `userPrompt` (or any other key) instead of `prompt`, a descriptor built to match this synthetic fixture can still pass this test while the live harness fails to extract the prompt. Conversely, if the descriptor correctly refuses to map an undocumented `prompt` field, this fixture will fail. In either case the fixture is wrong for a change whose stated policy is to keep third-party facts unverified.","digest":"622147649d4b8cb6","location":"tests/fixtures/harness/grok/prompt.json:17","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/fixtures/harness/grok/prompt.json:17"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"This test hardcodes the `\"copilot\"` normalizer when normalizing the Grok `pre_tool` fixture, instead of using the Grok descriptor's configured normalizer (`hookio.plan_for(\"grok\").normalizer`, as the preceding test does). Therefore it does not actually verify the Grok descriptor: if `hookio.plan_for(\"grok\").normalizer` is `\"claude\"` (consistent with `H.hooks.style == \"claude\"`) or is changed away from `\"copilot\"`, this test still exercises the Copilot normalizer and can pass even when the real Grok normalizer fails to extract `tool`. That gives false confidence that Grok tool events carry the tool name.","digest":"adcc3d9d608ff239","location":"tests/test_harness_grok_hooks.py:test_tool_event_carries_the_tool_name","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_harness_grok_hooks.py:test_tool_event_carries_the_tool_name"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":15938,"diff_sha":"5433117f27780d15996516cdd01d33436ef1a2b6afcd6208ade9713c245e5e26","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":513.4,"excluded_bytes":2144,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"f1704ceac450b04d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-grok-hook-descriptor.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261030T173930Z-8e25a55c.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-DX-grok-hook-descriptor-7267fe reviewed impl-grok-descriptor's DX-grok-hook-descriptor","reviewed_head":"8457c03c3bede1dbf5a37e3340121f3b7a3bfc68","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 97c011dbb5fab49f9e213052498615eb567a0e11","ddflow/harnesses/grok.toml":"100644 864572a871705b9d0cf3148795c3000b2fcf0eb5","ddflow/templates/drivers/deltas/grok-build.md":"100644 e12d6a8a0ce8d878e1940fd48ee4cb65a32af99e","tests/fixtures/harness/grok/post_tool.json":"100644 c960e2a1325c6ae612f09d72e2a6c5953c9293ba","tests/fixtures/harness/grok/pre_compact.json":"100644 6afbc2e